      "description": "Watch Colchester vs Southampton highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 8, 2026. The Carabao Cup delivered a night of intense tactical battles and late drama as Colchester United hosted Southampton in a high-stakes knockout encounter. Local Resilience in the First Half On 2026-08-08 , the home side entered the fray with no intention of playing the underdog role. Colchester United started with high energy, creating the first real threats of the match. Bradley Ihionvien and Jack Payne both saw efforts saved by Daniel Peretz , who was kept busy in the opening twenty minutes. While Southampton controlled much of the ball, their attempts from Kuryu Matsuki and Lewis Dobbin lacked the precision needed to break down a well-organized home defense, leading to a stalemate at the break. The Saints Intensify the Pressure Following the interval, the momentum shifted heavily in favor of the visitors. Southampton emerged with renewed intent, pinning Colchester United back into their own defensive third. Léo Scienza and Flynn Downes tested the resolve of the home side with several blocked shots, while goalkeeper Thimothée Lo-Tutala produced a fine save to deny a header from Taylor Harwood-Bellis . The introduction of Cyle Larin past the hour mark proved to be the tactical masterstroke the Premier League side required to find the breakthrough. Decisive Strike and Late Insurance The deadlock was finally broken in the 72nd minute. A pinpoint cross from Ryan Manning found Cyle Larin in the heart of the box, and the Canadian forward made no mistake, powering a header into the bottom corner. Despite a late surge from Colchester United , including a close-range header from Harry Anderson that flew just over the bar, the visitors held firm. In stoppage time, Romeo Akachukwu capitalized on a brilliant through ball from Finn Azaz to slot home a second goal, securing Southampton ’s progress and silencing the home crowd at the death."
